{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.BarTDualitySubstrate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.BarTDualitySubstrate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar_t_duality_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar_t_duality_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bar-t-duality-substrate.lean#L86-L100","doc":"**Substrate-level bar T-duality** (Proposition):\n\nThe bar involution bar : ℝ → ℝ on the substrate parameter is\nself-inverse, fixes 1, and is order-reversing on positives.\nAny zero of a \"discriminant\" function f at q = a is bar-paired\nto a zero of f ∘ bar at q = a⁻¹. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:bar-t-duality-substrate","label":"prop:bar-t-duality-substrate","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bar-t-duality-substrate.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar_paired_zero_locus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar_paired_zero_locus","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bar-t-duality-substrate.lean#L76-L84","doc":"A discriminant function f : ℝ → ℝ has a \"bar-paired zero locus\":\nif f(a) = 0 then (f ∘ bar)(a⁻¹) = 0. This is the abstract content\nof the bar T-duality on discriminants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar_lt_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar_lt_iff","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bar-t-duality-substrate.lean#L69-L74","doc":"Bar is order-reversing on positives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar_fixed_point_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar_fixed_point_pos","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bar-t-duality-substrate.lean#L51-L67","doc":"The unique positive fixed point of bar is 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar_pos","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bar-t-duality-substrate.lean#L45-L49","doc":"Bar maps positives to positives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar_one","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bar-t-duality-substrate.lean#L39-L43","doc":"Bar fixes 1: bar 1 = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bar-t-duality-substrate.lean#L33-L37","doc":"The bar involution is an involution on nonzero reals. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BarTDualitySubstrate.bar","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/bar-t-duality-substrate.lean#L30-L31","doc":"The bar involution on the multiplicative group ℝˣ. ","signatureChunk":0}]}